    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs73sH_D",
      "title": "validation: remove legacy kona prestates from standard list",
      "author": "claude",
      "number": 1296,
      "body": "<!-- ccr-slack-attribution -->\n_Requested by **Adrian Sutton** · [Slack thread](https://oplabs-pbc.slack.com/archives/C07LZR2JM88/p1785275474188729?thread_ts=1785275474.188729&cid=C07LZR2JM88)_\n\nRemoves the six legacy kona versions (1.1.6, 1.1.7, 1.2.2, 1.2.4, 1.2.5, 1.2.7) from the standard prestates list — none were ever a real release and no chain uses them.\n\nCompanion to an optimism PR that stops rebuilding these prestates in the reproducibility job. The two must merge together, or the scheduled job's reverse-check fails on entries that are still expected but no longer built.\n\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01PzWoQUHgwBxxAXesY3NDLt)_",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
